== Li 1,1

The following identity is true #display-equation($"Li"_(1\,1)\(x\,y\)= "Li"_2 (frac(x y - y, 1 - y)) - "Li"_2 (frac(y, y - 1)) - "Li"_2\(x y\)$) #display-equation($"Li"_2\(1 - x\)= - "Li" 2\(x\)- log x log\(1 - x\)+ pi^2 / 6$) Note that $log x log\(1 - x\)arrow.r 0$ as $x arrow.r 1$

#display-equation($"Li"_(1\,1)\(x\,y\) & = integral frac(d y, 1 - y) frac(d x, 1 - x) + frac(d\(x y\), 1 - x y) (frac(d y, 1 - y) - frac(d x, x\(1 - x\)))\
 & = integral d log\(1 - y\)d log\(1 - x\)+ d log\(1 - x y\)d log frac(x\(1 - y\), 1 - x)\
 & = integral d v_2 d v_1 + d v_12 d w_1$) To compute the monodromy around $x = 0$, take $q\(epsilon.alt\)$ to be the loop $\(x = epsilon.alt e^(i t)\,y = epsilon.alt\)$, we get $0$. \ To compute the monodromy around $y = 0$, take $q\(epsilon.alt\)$ to be the loop $\(x = epsilon.alt\,y = epsilon.alt e^(i t)\)$, we get $0$. \ To compute the monodromy around $x = 1$, take $q\(epsilon.alt\)$ to be the composition of $\(x =\(1 - t\)epsilon.alt + t\(1 - epsilon.alt\)\,y = epsilon.alt\)$, $\(x = 1 - epsilon.alt e^(i t)\,y = epsilon.alt\)$ and $\(x =\(1 - t\)\(1 - epsilon.alt\)+ t epsilon.alt\,y = epsilon.alt\)$, we get $0$. \ To compute the monodromy around $y = 1$, take $q\(epsilon.alt\)$ to be the composition of $\(x = epsilon.alt\,y =\(1 - t\)epsilon.alt + t\(1 - epsilon.alt\)\)$, $\(x = epsilon.alt\,y = 1 - epsilon.alt e^(i t)\)$ and $\(x = epsilon.alt\,y =\(1 - t\)\(1 - epsilon.alt\)+ t epsilon.alt\)$, we get $- 2 pi i "Li"_1\(x\)$. \ To compute the monodromy around $x y = 1$, take $q$ to be the loop $\(x = x^0\,y upright(" such that ") integral_q d log\(1 - x y\)= 2 pi i\)$, we get $- 2 pi i "Li"_1\(frac(1 - x y, 1 - x)\)$

The variation matrix is #display-equation($Lambda = mat(delim: "[", 1, , , ; "Li"_1\(y\), 1, , ; "Li"_1\(x y\), , 1, ; "Li"_(1\,1)\(x\,y\), "Li"_1\(x\), "Li"_1 (frac(1 - x y, 1 - x)), 1) tau_(1\,1)\(2 pi i\)$) #display-equation($omega = mat(delim: "[", 0, , , ; - d v_2, 0, , ; - d v_12, 0, 0, ; 0, - d v_1, - d w_1, 0)$) Note that $"Li"_1 (frac(1 - x y, 1 - x)) = - log (frac(x\(y - 1\), 1 - x)) = "Li"_1\(y\)- "Li"_1\(x^(- 1)\)= "Li"_1\(y\)- "Li"_1\(x\)- log x - i pi$ \ The monodromy representation $rho$ is as follows \ For monodromy around $x = 0$ #display-equation($mat(delim: "[", 1, , , ; #none, 1, , ; #none, , 1, ; #none, , - 1, 1)$) For monodromy around $y = 0$, identity. \ For monodromy around $x = 1$ #display-equation($mat(delim: "[", 1, , , ; #none, 1, , ; #none, , 1, ; #none, - 1, 1, 1)$) For monodromy around $y = 1$ #display-equation($mat(delim: "[", 1, , , ; - 1, 1, , ; #none, , 1, ; #none, , - 1, 1)$) For monodromy around $x y = 1$ #display-equation($mat(delim: "[", 1, , , ; #none, 1, , ; - 1, , 1, ; #none, , , 1)$)

$hat(cal(L))_(1\,1)\(x\)= "Li"_(1\,1)\(x\,y\)- 1 / 2 v_12 v_2 - 1 / 2 v_1 v_2 + 1 / 2 v_1 v_12 - 1 / 2 u_1 v_12$
